00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.540 align:start position:0%
grouping is used when the data we have  is very large and the groups are called  class intervals in one of our examples  we had seen groups like these 1 2 5 6 to  10 11 to 15 and so on there are a few  things we need to know about class  intervals the class intervals should be  non-overlapping it means that the same  number cannot be present in two or more  groups one number should belong to just  one group all the groups should exhaust  all the data we have with us these three  groups are enough to cover all marks  from 1 to 15 but if we had someone who  scored a 16 these three groups would not  be enough  next the class size or the class width  should be the same class width is the  difference between the two lower limits  or two upper limits of continuous class  intervals so 6 minus 1 should equal 11  minus 6 and 10 minus 5 and 15 minus 10  should also be equal  remember they shouldn't be overlapping  the intervals should cover all values in  the data and the class width has to be  the same throughout there is just one  more condition we need to keep in mind  in the first interval 1 &amp; 5 are class  limits and the average of 1 &amp; 5 is  called the class mark the fourth  condition says that the class limits and  the class marks of each interval should  be integers or simple fractions a simple  fraction is a fraction in which the  numerator and the denominator are both  integers these are the basic rules we  need to keep in mind while making groups  or class intervals
 

